{"schema":"clawhub.skill.verify.v1","ok":true,"decision":"pass","reasons":[],"slug":"hubspot-ops","displayName":"HubSpot","pageUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/hith3sh/skills/hubspot-ops","publisherHandle":"hith3sh","publisherDisplayName":"Jay","publisherProfileUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/hith3sh","version":"1.0.5","resolvedFrom":"version","tag":null,"createdAt":1780989104739,"card":{"available":true,"path":"skill-card.md","url":"https://wry-manatee-359.convex.site/api/v1/skills/hubspot-ops/card?ownerHandle=hith3sh&version=1.0.5","sha256":"88b2ac855738b8a0a4a4737564a00d65c435bef8426c3779d94714e4c5525bb8","size":2378,"contentType":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8"},"artifact":{"sourceFingerprint":"f52b68a7c1968803504cf5d2e00c5e82fd28c6f42858865e9ddc2f0a65f82438","bundleFingerprints":["af11677c17f488d32eee9843d67660c8f195976a5b6573e0c9bd571cc1db751e","ff72f22689ee5c2e40bf847dc6c682a5e07ee6f9e9ecbce679c156789c31152c"],"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":21272,"sha256":"6581bd198ddb6d948777afd9eda1bdf793ef2d7e0ab183ddccee7573233cdd61","contentType":"text/markdown"}]},"provenance":{"source":"unavailable","reason":"No server-resolved GitHub import provenance is stored for this version."},"security":{"status":"clean","passed":true,"rawStatus":"clean","verdict":"benign","confidence":"high","summary":"This HubSpot skill is a disclosed CRM integration, but users should only install it if they trust ClawLink and are comfortable granting HubSpot write access.","model":null,"checkedAt":1789544992010,"scannerReports":{"aig":{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.1","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[{"ruleId":"T08","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Unpinned Privileged External Plugin Installation"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"SKILL.md"},"region":{"startLine":47,"endLine":49}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"fd7ee79701aa8d50"},"properties":{"description":"## Vulnerability Details\n\n**File Location**: `SKILL.md`, lines 47–49; repeated at lines 455–456  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Unpinned third-party dependency with privileged tool access  \n**Risk Level**: Medium\n\n```bash\nopenclaw plugins install clawhub:clawlink-plugin\nopenclaw config set tools.alsoAllow '[\"clawlink-plugin\"]' --strict-json\nopenclaw gateway restart\n```\n\nThe equivalent configuration and restart commands are repeated in the troubleshooting instructions:\n\n```bash\nopenclaw config set tools.alsoAllow '[\"clawlink-plugin\"]' --strict-json\nopenclaw gateway restart\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe skill instructs users to install `clawlink-plugin` from an external package registry without specifying an immutable version, content digest, or signature-verification procedure. It then adds the plugin to the tool allowlist and restarts the OpenClaw gateway, causing the externally supplied implementation to become active.\n\nThe audited project contains only `SKILL.md`; it does not include the plugin source, lock metadata, checksums, or reproducible build information. Consequently, the behavior of the installed component—including its treatment of OAuth tokens, proxied HubSpot requests, and CRM data—cannot be statically verified from this package.\n\nThis creates a supply-chain exposure: the artifact installed in the future may differ from the artifact that was reviewed. Exploitation would require compromise, replacement, or malicious publication of the referenced plugin package or its distribution infrastructure.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. An attacker compromises the plugin publisher account, package registry, build pipeline, or distribution artifact.\n2. The attacker publishes a modified release under the referenced unversioned package name.\n3. A user follows the skill instructions and installs the current package using:\n   `openclaw plugins install clawhub:clawlink-plugin`.\n4. The user explicitly enables the plugin through `tools.alsoAllow`.\n5. The gateway restarts and loads the compromised plugin.\n6. The malicious plugin can execute within its granted plugin context and intercept or manipulate subsequent ClawLink and HubSpot workflows.\n7. Depending on the runtime permissions and connected HubSpot account, it could expose CRM information or initiate unauthorized operations.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nA compromised dependency could obtain the privileges granted to the enabled plugin and affect HubSpot integration workflows. Potential scope includes access to data made available through the connected account, interception of OAuth-backed requests, alteration of CRM operations, and disclosure of contacts, companies, deals, tickets, marketing information, or related records.\n\nThe exact operating-system privileges and token accessibility cannot be established from `SKILL.md`, because the plugin implementation and runtime permission model are outside the audited project. The impact is therefore conditional on the permissions granted by OpenClaw, ClawLink, and the connected HubSpot user.","severity":"Medium"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Pin the plugin to an immutable, reviewed version and preferably a cryptographic content digest.\n2. Document and enforce package-signature or checksum verification before installation.\n3. Provide a verifiable source repository, release provenance, and reproducible build information for the plugin.\n4. Maintain a dependency lock or equivalent integrity metadata in the skill package.\n5. Require explicit user approval before plugin installation, allowlist modification, and gateway restart.\n6. Apply least privilege to the plugin and connected HubSpot account, limiting OAuth scopes to the features actually required.\n7. Separate read-only and write-capable permissions where supported.\n8. Record and monitor plugin installation, upgrades, OAuth access, and CRM write operations.\n9. Review new plugin releases before updating rather than automatically resolving an unversioned package to the latest artifact."}}]}],"properties":{"securityScore":75,"primaryLanguage":"Markdown","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1789544918.6910014,"endTime":1789544960.2043898}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"hubspot-ops","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v57enx6e35g5p8kz1y6336qb618eg0ah-kqRQAp/clawscan-skillspector-3156042764/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-09-16T07:48:34.690695+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":0,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","max_issue_severity":"NONE"},"components":[{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":479,"executable":false,"size_bytes":21272,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[],"suppressed_count":0,"suppressed":[],"metadata":{"has_executable_scripts":false,"skillspector_version":"2.11.2","llm_requested":true,"llm_available":true,"meta_analysis_applied":false,"inference_usage":[{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":7798,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":7812},{"node":"semantic_quality_policy","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":7838,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":7852},{"node":"semantic_security_discovery","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":7370,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":7384}],"filtering_mode":"heuristic","llm_calls_attempted":3,"llm_calls_succeeded":3},"execution_successful":true,"analysis_completeness":{"total_components":1,"scanned_components":1,"coverage_percent":100,"is_complete":false,"status":"partial","execution_successful":true,"fully_inspected_files":1,"partially_inspected_files":0,"entirely_un